Package: RAssistant
Title: A Lightweight AI Assistant for RStudio
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: person("MySimpleSmart", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "120612480+MySimpleSmart@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Opens the existing Source-aware chat assistant in the RStudio
    Viewer. Supports image uploads, optional live console context, contextual R help,
    project course knowledge (lecture PDFs, notes, R examples and custom instructions),
    reviewed Source edits and explicitly approved script validation. Stores optional credentials
    in the operating system credential store, separately from package updates.
License: file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.2.0)
Imports:
    askpass,
    callr,
    commonmark,
    ellmer (>= 0.5.0),
    htmltools,
    jsonlite,
    keyring (>= 1.3.0),
    knitr,
    later,
    remotes,
    rlang,
    rstudioapi,
    shiny (>= 1.14.0)
Suggests:
    pdftools
URL: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant
BugReports: https://github.com/MySimpleSmart/RAssistant/issues
Config/RAssistant/Changes: Extra blank lines are spacing, not errors. Spacing-only edits stay out of automatic fixes and need explicit inclusion.
    Keep a local edit history with exact before/after code, and preview Undo before restoring an AI change. Manual edits block Undo.
    Optional Workspace context reads object types, dimensions and column names without sending data rows.
    Explain, fix or improve the current R chunk in Rmd/Quarto while preserving other chunks, fences and prose.
